From 89192251c8c618fb7f46e755695621b663e878d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:00:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): optimize TileLang indexer, sparse MLA, front,
 mHC, and column kernels

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
with candidate-55's series applied through 0810.

Rationale: Accelerates prefill attention and front-end kernels on SM121 via
split-K indexer scoring, fused front/mHC and column operations, and sparse MLA
scheduling/staging refinements while keeping visible-slot indexer bounds and
compute-sanitizer initcheck/memcheck/synccheck/racecheck clean.

Quality implications: None; numerical accuracy and visible-slot isolation match
reference PyTorch implementations.

Tests: pytest -q -p deepseek_models tests/kernels/attention/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang.py
plus compute-sanitizer (memcheck, synccheck, initcheck, racecheck).

Upstream status: local candidate-60 patch
